==Trivia==
* Momoiro Clover Z, the idol group that performed this song, filmed a music video to accompany it. In the video, the five girls dance while wearing {{p|Charmander}}, {{p|Jigglypuff}}, {{p|Croagunk}}, {{p|Bulbasaur}}, and {{p|Pikachu}} costumes. All five of these Pokémon can be seen in the fourth Japanese ending animation of {{aniseries|BW}}, which uses their song.
* The song itself can be played in the Japanese {{wp|Just Dance Wii U}} game by Ubisoft. It is said to be Medium Level, and the coach is a girl disguised as a cat. The dance actually copies {{an|Meloetta}}'s dance in the ending.
* This is the first Japanese opening or ending theme not to be published by [[Pikachu Records]], due to {{wp|Media Factory}}'s acquisition by {{wp|Kadokawa Corporation|Kadokawa}} in October 2011. All subsequent ending themes until [[Ready Go]] would instead be published by an imprint of {{wp|Sony Music Entertainment Japan|Sony Music Japan}}.
** It is also the only song excluded from the Selected Edition of [[Pokémon TV Anime Theme Song BEST OF BEST OF BEST 1997-2023]] that was made available digitally, as {{wp|King Records}} had already made it available on the album [[Maiden War]].

